WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.170 --> 00:00:06.310
Can you imagine Usopp becoming one of the
most important characters in the story? Fulfilling

00:00:06.310 --> 00:00:13.670
prophecies, acquiring conqueror's Haki and
taking out one of the Yonko? No? Well, I can.

00:00:13.670 --> 00:00:19.029
I think that after Whole Cake Island being
Sanji's arc and Wano being Zoro's arc, Elbaf

00:00:19.029 --> 00:00:25.130
will be the arc of God Usopp, where the cowardly,
insecure and lying boy from Syrup Village

00:00:25.130 --> 00:00:31.199
will become one of the fiercest and bravest
warriors the endless seas of one piece have

00:00:31.199 --> 00:00:39.860
ever seen. So let me now share with you the
gospel of the the almighty and all-knowing

00:00:39.860 --> 00:00:41.969
God of sniper island.

00:00:41.969 --> 00:00:49.010
Hi there, I'm Manu and Usopp has always held
a very special place in my heart out of any

00:00:49.010 --> 00:00:50.620
fictional character. Rarely have I ever changed
my mind about someone as drastically as this

00:00:50.620 --> 00:00:53.190
obnoxious boy, Luffy decides to recruit into
his crew. I want to walk you through his incredible

00:00:53.190 --> 00:00:59.499
character arc until Wano that turned him into
one of the most-beloved characters in fiction

00:00:59.499 --> 00:01:05.600
and then share a number of carefully-selected
exquisite theories with you, that might foreshadow

00:01:05.600 --> 00:01:10.390
some major developments for Usopp and his
powers, very soon.

00:01:10.390 --> 00:01:15.810
Usopp is an incredibly interesting character
in a multitude of ways. Take his name for

00:01:15.810 --> 00:01:21.030
example. Usopp is a combination of the famous
greek storyteller and fabulist Aesopp and

00:01:21.030 --> 00:01:27.030
the Japanese word uso, that literally means
lie. Oda clearly was fully aware of where

00:01:27.030 --> 00:01:33.170
he wanted the character to go. Because Usopp
is both, a great liar and a fantastic story

00:01:33.170 --> 00:01:34.770
teller and to me it shows how well-planned
and consistent he was written. On top of that,

00:01:34.770 --> 00:01:41.420
he is by far the most 'normal' member in a
crew of absolute monsters, making it super

00:01:41.420 --> 00:01:45.659
easy for me to relate to his experience traveling
with the straw hats.

00:01:45.659 --> 00:01:50.890
I was incredibly impressed, how well established
these fundamental traits were established

00:01:50.890 --> 00:01:55.829
in Syrup village, where we first get to meet
Usopp. Immediately you and I know, that this

00:01:55.829 --> 00:02:02.679
is someone who craves attention above all
else. He lies and exaggerates to any- and

00:02:02.679 --> 00:02:08.590
everyone he meets, just to have people notice
him. The way he deceives the villagers that

00:02:08.590 --> 00:02:15.790
pirates are coming until no one believes him,
is literally the story of Peter and the wolf.

00:02:15.790 --> 00:02:21.120
This deceptiveness and pretentiousness in
everything he says and does made Usopp immediately

00:02:21.120 --> 00:02:28.560
unlikable to me. However, a little later , we
find out why. Usopp is basically an Orphan.

00:02:28.560 --> 00:02:34.569
His mother died when he was young and his
father left him to become a pirate. Now to

00:02:34.569 --> 00:02:40.049
be fair, it was Shanks who is fighting for
a better world, and I don't think Yasopp is

00:02:40.049 --> 00:02:45.540
a bad person from what we have seen of him,
but let's be real, he doesn't deserve a father

00:02:45.540 --> 00:02:48.330
of the year award for it either.

00:02:48.330 --> 00:02:54.269
In my eyes, this left Usopp with 2 choices:
Resent his father for leaving or, as he did

00:02:54.269 --> 00:03:00.750
in the end, glorified him. After all why,
would he leave his kid behind if he wasn't

00:03:00.750 --> 00:03:06.939
a legendary pirate with important work to
do? This really hits home hard, when you realize

00:03:06.939 --> 00:03:13.550
that it's probably this insecurity about being
left behind, that lead to Usopp's chronic

00:03:13.550 --> 00:03:20.489
lying. He lies about being a great and powerful
man, having had many adventures, just like

00:03:20.489 --> 00:03:29.060
his father, because he feels like he can never
be this person in reality. He feels weak,

00:03:29.060 --> 00:03:35.030
insecure and worthless. His worst side. Keep
that in mind for water seven.

00:03:35.030 --> 00:03:40.689
At the same time however, I love that we also
get introduced to Usopp's best side. On the

00:03:40.689 --> 00:03:56.159
sickbeds of his dying mother and of his friend
Kaya, he also fabricates stories. However,

00:03:56.159 --> 00:04:00.909
while his usual lies are meant for getting
himself some attention, these stories are

00:04:00.909 --> 00:04:07.049
meant to brighten up the day of people he
cares about. It's the story-teller inside

00:04:07.049 --> 00:04:13.219
him, caring for others. And to me, it is exactly
this altruism that is the basis for Usopp

00:04:13.219 --> 00:04:21.290
becoming a brave warrior of the sea. And according
to the theories I have in store for you, he

00:04:21.290 --> 00:04:23.341
will be a great warrior indeed.

00:04:23.341 --> 00:04:32.820
In Arlong Park, during his fight with Chu,
he finds his dream, to become a brave warrior

00:04:32.820 --> 00:04:40.190
of the sea. But honestly, I do believe, that
Usopp is brave right from the beginning. Usopp’s

00:04:40.190 --> 00:04:46.690
cowardice is actually very self-imposed. Effectively,
it is another one of his lies. This even links

00:04:46.690 --> 00:04:51.790
to the concept of him telling lies that later
become true. Usopp’s self-doubt acts as

00:04:51.790 --> 00:04:56.280
what is called a ‘self-fulfilling prophecy’.
Even though he is often scared, in the end

00:04:56.280 --> 00:05:01.980
he always decides to stay, fight and do the
right thing. He has shown time and time again,

00:05:01.980 --> 00:05:06.690
that when it really counts, he is undeniably
brave, proud, and honourable. He even goes

00:05:06.690 --> 00:05:10.250
on to defeat Chu, a fishmen way stronger than
him. So to me, his arc is not about becoming

00:05:10.250 --> 00:05:17.030
brave, because bravery requires fear to be
overcome, no to me his real arc is about building

00:05:17.030 --> 00:05:21.470
confidence, accepting himself and finding
a purpose.

00:05:21.470 --> 00:05:28.210
The next big step in his character arc is
during Alabasta. I couldn't help but be impressed,

00:05:28.210 --> 00:05:32.840
how he overcomes his fear to be hurt, and
once again steps out against an opponent he

00:05:32.840 --> 00:05:40.590
thinks is way out of his league. He is willing
to give his life for his captain and declares

00:05:40.590 --> 00:05:42.780
his loyalty for Luffy.

00:05:42.780 --> 00:05:48.580
Interestingly enough, just a while later,
we experience Usopp's lowest point in the

00:05:48.580 --> 00:05:54.840
story. I'd argue that his fight with Luffy
and his leaving the crew doesn't diminish

00:05:54.840 --> 00:06:00.330
his believe that Luffy will be pirate king.
The going Merry, the ship they had been given

00:06:00.330 --> 00:06:05.900
by his village, had become a member of the
crew, to the point where Usopp could even

00:06:05.900 --> 00:06:12.500
see a manifestation of its will, something
that will be important later on by the way.

00:06:12.500 --> 00:06:17.840
Conquerors haki. Now, this member of the crew
had gotten too weak to fulfil its purpose

00:06:17.840 --> 00:06:24.270
and was about to be left behind by the rest.
Usopp sees himself to be the next in line.

00:06:24.270 --> 00:06:29.880
Despite all the courage he has shown, he still
has the worlds biggest impostor syndrome.

00:06:29.880 --> 00:06:35.490
The same reason why he tried to forcibly put
himself on a level with Luffy. This is hammered

00:06:35.490 --> 00:06:49.830
home by this scene here. [you are not a shipwright
usopp] Usopp is the only one, that doesn't

00:06:49.830 --> 00:06:55.250
have a fixed role in the crew yet. He is not
recognised as the sniper of the crew at this

00:06:55.250 --> 00:07:00.750
point. Only during Enies Lobby, does he come
back as Sogeking, a representation of everything

00:07:00.750 --> 00:07:06.430
Usopp thinks he wants to be. He hides behind
a mask, that allows him to slip into a more

00:07:06.430 --> 00:07:11.090
confined persona. As a result, his actions
on Enies Lobby establish him as the sniper

00:07:11.090 --> 00:07:16.000
of the crew and after witnessing the lengths
Luffy would go to to keep a crew member for

00:07:16.000 --> 00:07:24.650
robin, he overcomes his fear of being left
behind and apologizes.

00:07:24.650 --> 00:07:36.120
Thriller bark proves to us though, how insecure
Usopp still is, even under the mask of Sogeking,

00:07:36.120 --> 00:07:39.610
while once again taking down a strong opponent.

00:07:39.610 --> 00:07:47.140
I was very positively surprised to see, that
Dressrosa out of all places, was Usopp's biggest

00:07:47.140 --> 00:07:52.710
moment of character development yet. The tontatta
put all their hopes into Usopp, thinking that

00:07:52.710 --> 00:07:58.200
there hero Usolando will come help them. The
stress for Usopp in this arc has been building

00:07:58.200 --> 00:08:03.650
up steadily and in the end he couldn’t handle
the pressure of his responsibility he caused

00:08:03.650 --> 00:08:11.570
with his own lies,so he runs away. Unfortunately
Usopp represents one of the main themes of

00:08:11.570 --> 00:08:18.730
Dressrosa here, deception. All this time Doflamingo
had been deceiving the tontatta and Usopp

00:08:18.730 --> 00:08:26.010
was essentially doing the same. However in
the end their cries finally reach Usopp. Without

00:08:26.010 --> 00:08:31.600
Sogeking to hide behind, he finally accepts
himself as a true and strong member of the

00:08:31.600 --> 00:08:39.779
straw hat crew. [announces that he is Usopp
of the strawhat pirates] Usopp gains confidence

00:08:39.779 --> 00:08:45.769
in himself and his capabilities to be a real
hero and is rewarded immensely for it with

00:08:45.769 --> 00:08:58.509
one of my favourite moments after the time
skip. As a result, the Usopp we see in Wano,

00:08:58.509 --> 00:09:03.959
is the most confident, but also most competent
version of him, we have ever seen, turning

00:09:03.959 --> 00:09:06.279
the tides wherever he appears.

00:09:06.279 --> 00:09:11.370
So now that I want to move on to Usopp's future
in the story, what's important to know is

00:09:11.370 --> 00:09:17.870
that Usopp keeps fulfilling many of his major
lies one after another, becoming more and

00:09:17.870 --> 00:09:22.589
more the hero he aspires to be.

00:09:22.589 --> 00:09:28.459
As always, everything from here on out is
speculation based on my previous analysis,

00:09:28.459 --> 00:09:35.490
but I'm excited about all these possibilities.
And as you probably already suspected, Elbaf

00:09:35.490 --> 00:09:41.740
will be the bases for all these theories.
Elbaf spelled backwards after all is fable,

00:09:41.740 --> 00:09:47.519
and I think I might become the most important
arc for our story telling fable master yet.

00:09:47.519 --> 00:09:52.860
Throughout the story, Usopp has forget relationships
with the giants he met.

00:09:52.860 --> 00:09:57.670
First on Little Garden with Dory and Broggy,
that inspire him to become like the giant

00:09:57.670 --> 00:10:03.850
warriors, inspiring his dream and promising
to go to Elbaf. On Enies Lobby he frees Oimo

00:10:03.850 --> 00:10:09.050
and Kashi from their bonds to the world government,
perfectly reciting the giants weapons and

00:10:09.050 --> 00:10:19.990
techniques []. 

00:10:19.990 --> 00:10:25.490
Once again he promises to meet them in Elbaf.
And finally he gains the respect of Hajrudin

00:10:25.490 --> 00:10:32.370
on Dressrosa, who declares him a god, giving
Usopp a very high standing across multiple

00:10:32.370 --> 00:10:35.060
generations among the giants of Elbaf.

00:10:35.060 --> 00:10:45.389
The first lie I want to look at is this [Descendant
of noland].

00:10:45.389 --> 00:10:50.920
As I have discussed in my big one piece theory,
Noland is actually one of the most influential

00:10:50.920 --> 00:10:58.329
characters in the entire story and a direct
parallel to Roger himself. Outside of Shandora,

00:10:58.329 --> 00:11:04.160
Noland traveled the New World multiple times
and is worshiped by the tontatta. Usopp is

00:11:04.160 --> 00:11:10.449
tied to Noland through the two statues he
has, one in Shandora and one in Dressrosa.

00:11:10.449 --> 00:11:16.560
And so I think it would make a lot of sense
for Noland to also have been to Elbaf. A popular

00:11:16.560 --> 00:11:23.260
idea is that Usopp will defeat Loki, the current
ruler of Elbaf, which would fit Usopp's arc

00:11:23.260 --> 00:11:29.779
perfectly. A great reference to David vs Goliath.
A legend in which the small David defeated

00:11:29.779 --> 00:11:34.870
the giant Goliath with a slingshot. And I
don't find it too far fetched to theroize

00:11:34.870 --> 00:11:38.880
that Usopp might find out his relationship
to Noland here as well.

00:11:38.880 --> 00:11:45.600
If this were true, this could have some major
implications for Usopp. It is quite possible

00:11:45.600 --> 00:11:51.490
that Noland, just like Roger, was one of the
people who inherited Joy Boys will, while

00:11:51.490 --> 00:11:56.519
failing to keep the promises they made. Other
characters that might fall into this line

00:11:56.519 --> 00:12:03.759
are Binks and Nika. And the sun god was actually
mentioned the first time during Nolands flashback.

00:12:03.759 --> 00:12:09.059
And as you know, Usopp has also earned the
status of god. If this were true, it would

00:12:09.059 --> 00:12:14.649
not be Luffy, but Usopp who would be the inheritor
of Joyboys will, setting him up to be the

00:12:14.649 --> 00:12:22.259
liberator of the Giants. Now, I DO think that
Luffy is Joyboy, but I DID find this line

00:12:22.259 --> 00:12:28.389
of thought very entertaining. And even if
Usopp was JUST a dependent of Noland, that

00:12:28.389 --> 00:12:31.559
would already be awesome by itself.

00:12:31.559 --> 00:12:36.209
Next let's look at something that has been
hinted at a lot throughout the story: Usopp

00:12:36.209 --> 00:12:42.760
getting conqueror's haki. Yes you heard me
right. I'm suggesting that THE Usopp, our

00:12:42.760 --> 00:12:49.439
Usopp, might unlock what only Luffy and Zoro
have within the crew so far. So how does the

00:12:49.439 --> 00:12:55.990
ambition and will of a king fit together with
the king of cowards? Well the first clue is

00:12:55.990 --> 00:13:02.050
already in the name. Usopp has proclaimed
himself to be a powerful pirate captain throughout

00:13:02.050 --> 00:13:08.180
the story and wants to become a brave warrior
of the see. In a way he has these kingly ambitions

00:13:08.180 --> 00:13:14.399
in a more literal sense than even luffy or
zoro. As for willpower, I already have explained

00:13:14.399 --> 00:13:20.050
that to me Usopp has been brave and strong
willed from the start. The only thing holding

00:13:20.050 --> 00:13:26.020
Usopp back really are his self-doubts and
his self-image. However this is slowly melting

00:13:26.020 --> 00:13:31.890
away. Usopp has already unlocked one type
of haki and that on the most extreme level

00:13:31.890 --> 00:13:38.009
we have seen in the story so far, picking
out the exact aura of a person miles away

00:13:38.009 --> 00:13:39.009
from him.

00:13:39.009 --> 00:13:44.689
So, could there have been hints in the story?
Similarly to Zoro? I believe there is actually

00:13:44.689 --> 00:13:51.699
a ton of foreshadowing for this. Usopp has
actually lied about having conquers haki twice

00:13:51.699 --> 00:14:02.411
now. Once I this scene here with the tontatta
[underground shaking, actually my haki]. And

00:14:02.411 --> 00:14:07.480
a second time during the raid on onigashima.
Additionally, we have two instances where

00:14:07.480 --> 00:14:17.269
Usopp knocks out powerful opponents by literally
crushing their will. Once with sugar [] and

00:14:17.269 --> 00:14:27.180
once with Perona. Both times we can see the
characteristic foaming mouth, that is reserved

00:14:27.180 --> 00:14:30.149
for someone knocked out by conquerors haki.

00:14:30.149 --> 00:14:35.089
Conqueror’s Haki relates very much to one’s
spirit and spiritual presence, as well as

00:14:35.089 --> 00:14:41.259
to ones ability to affect the spirits of others.
And Usopp was originally the only one able

00:14:41.259 --> 00:14:46.759
to interact with the Going Merry’s Klabautermann.
So could this be another one of his lies coming

00:14:46.759 --> 00:14:53.360
true once Usopp reaches his full potential
in elbaf? Well I would lie if I told you I

00:14:53.360 --> 00:14:55.940
wouldn't absolutely love it.

00:14:55.940 --> 00:15:00.720
To round things up, now that we have a quite
powerful Usopp, the last theory I want to

00:15:00.720 --> 00:15:06.410
discuss has been proposed by a Reddit User
called africhic, who proposes that Usopp might

00:15:06.410 --> 00:15:12.540
be the one to bring an end to big mum's chase
after the straw hats. Shoutout to him.

00:15:12.540 --> 00:15:18.079
We have already talked about Usopp's relationship
with the giants. And Big mom shares this affinity

00:15:18.079 --> 00:15:22.959
with him. She has gone to great lengths to
include the giants into her piece project

00:15:22.959 --> 00:15:28.019
and has been inspired by their warrior spirit.
As you might have noticed, one of her main

00:15:28.019 --> 00:15:38.679
attacks is the same giant technique used by
Dory and Broggy. [Ikoku Sovereign] She uses

00:15:38.679 --> 00:15:44.339
it three times, ones on WHole Cake island,
once on the life floor in onigashima and once

00:15:44.339 --> 00:15:50.470
on the rooftop with kaido. And yet, funnily
enough, the only straw hat who hasn't experienced

00:15:50.470 --> 00:15:56.860
this attack yet, is Usopp, the man who knows
all of Dory's and Broggy's techniques. Both

00:15:56.860 --> 00:16:02.510
of these character arcs are on a collision
course for Elbaf and yet their standing among

00:16:02.510 --> 00:16:08.070
the Giants couldn’t be any farther apart.&nbsp;Big
Mom, who is seen as a force of destruction&nbsp;and

00:16:08.070 --> 00:16:15.559
usopp, who has been&nbsp;heralded as a warrior
and a God. So Usopp might well be the only

00:16:15.559 --> 00:16:20.350
person to end the feud between the straw hats
and big mom.

00:16:20.350 --> 00:16:24.869
To solidify all this, we're gonna have some
shenanigans with the chapter numbers again.

00:16:24.869 --> 00:16:30.029
You know I love those. This time however,
instead of the word plays we'll just rearrange

00:16:30.029 --> 00:16:36.420
some numbers, because Oda loves doing that.
For instance take the first panels of chapter

00:16:36.420 --> 00:16:43.790
592 and 925. Or 387 and 783.

00:16:43.790 --> 00:16:50.290
The chapter I want to look at is&nbsp;[Chapter
834 “My Dream”], that shows big mom talking

00:16:50.290 --> 00:16:57.740
about her dream to have the giants with her,
as well as&nbsp;[Chapter 483 “The End of the

00:16:57.740 --> 00:17:05.040
Dream”] which features Lola, the daughter
who ruined the wedding with Loki.

00:17:05.040 --> 00:17:10.430
Usopp has the opposite standing with the Giants
than Big Mom, two sides of the same coin.

00:17:10.430 --> 00:17:18.380
..what happens when we flip it?&nbsp;[Chapter
438...&nbsp;in which Usopp choses to return to

00:17:18.380 --> 00:17:21.780
the crew instead of his dream of going to
Elbaf.

00:17:21.780 --> 00:17:27.360
What blew my mind is that, actually no matter
which way you rearrange these three numbers

00:17:27.360 --> 00:17:32.790
it&nbsp;**always**&nbsp;has to do with characters
thinking they have to give up their dreams:

00:17:32.790 --> 00:17:38.340
348, the chapter that Robin chooses to go
with CP-9 in order to protect the Strawhats

00:17:38.340 --> 00:17:43.640
- giving up on her dream of learning the history
of the world and Saul’s last wish of finding

00:17:43.640 --> 00:17:47.930
her friends.
384, the chapter where Usopp tells Oimo and

00:17:47.930 --> 00:17:52.530
Kashii the truth. Moments before they thought
they had to give up on their dreams of seeing

00:17:52.530 --> 00:17:59.120
their captains again.
And 843, the chapter Sanji tells Luffy he’s

00:17:59.120 --> 00:18:05.030
leaving - giving up on his dream of the All
Blue in order to protect his friends.

00:18:05.030 --> 00:18:10.450
What will Usopp say, when he sees Big Mom's
attack? Will he say that he's friends with

00:18:10.450 --> 00:18:17.150
the giants, that he fought with them and has
Hajrudin as his underling? It would sound

00:18:17.150 --> 00:18:22.940
like the biggest lie ever but turn out to
be nothing but the truth.

00:18:22.940 --> 00:18:27.970
Another character that is strongly linked
to Elbaf and nordic mythology is none other

00:18:27.970 --> 00:18:35.930
than Shanks himself. If you want to know why,
I strongly recommend you check out that video

00:18:35.930 --> 00:18:38.049
right here.

